Roll No: 46
Algorithm: calculator using switch statement

          1.	Start
	2.	Declare three integer variables: num1, num2, choice
	3.	Display the message “Enter two numbers” and read values into num1 and num2
	4.	Display the menu:
	•		1.	Addition
	•		2.	Subtraction
	•		3.	Multiplication
	•		4.	Division
	5.	Prompt the user to “Enter your choice” and read the value into choice
	6.	Check the value of choice using a switch statement:
	•	If choice = 1:
a. Compute sum = num1 + num2
b. Display the sum
	•	If choice = 2:
a. Compute difference = num1 - num2
b. Display the difference
	•	If choice = 3:
a. Compute product = num1 * num2
b. Display the product
	•	If choice = 4:
a. Check if num2 ≠ 0
	•	If true: compute quotient = num1 / num2 and display it
	•	If false: display “Error! Division by zero is not allowed”
	•	Default (any other choice):
	•	Display “Error! Invalid choice”
	7.	Stop
